I may have got indexing working on an old i3 without "avx2" and "fma" following these steps:
1) build lancedb (the nodejs part) with just the relevant cpu features (in my case "avx");
2) patch the code @Patrick-Erichsen added to detect old cpu (or rather cpu with missing features): core/config/util.ts function isSupportedLanceDbCpuTarget to make it return true;
3) build continue as per CONTRIBUTING.md;
4) unzip the packaged .vsix file (which is just a zipfile) and replace "extension/out/node_modules/@lancedb/vectordb-linux-x64-gnu/index.node" with lancedb/nodejs/dist/lancedb.linux-x64-gnu.node from step 1 (renamed to index.node);
5) zip back the unzipped .vsix;
6) install the extension and enjoy lastest continue (0.9.259 at the time I'm writing this) with indexing working nicely.

There are much clever ways to deal with the dependency than forcing the lancedb nodejs binary but I'm not a nodejs person myself, however the steps above can easily be scripted or turned into ci/cd tasks.
